\fs14 \

\fs28 You can check whether formatted strings conform to the entry types of cells with the 
\b isEntryAcceptable:
\b0  method. NSControl subclasses also use 
\b isEntryAcceptable:
\b0  to validate what users have typed in editable cells. You can control the format of values accepted and displayed in cells by creating a custom subclass of NSFormatter and associating an instance of that class with cells (through 
\b setFormatter:
\b0 ). In custom NSCell subclasses, you can also override 
\b isEntryAcceptable:
\b0  to check for the validity of data entered into cells.\

