\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Invoked by an NSControl to initiate the tracking behavior of one of its NSCells. It's generally not overriden since the default implementation invokes other NSCell methods that can be overriden to handle specific events in a dragging session. Returns YES if the mouse goes up within 
\i cellFrame
\i0 , NO otherwise. The argument 
\i theEvent
\i0  is typically the mouse event received by the initiating NSControl, usually identified by 
\i controlView
\i0 . The 
\i flag
\i0  argument indicates whether tracking should continue until the mouse button goes up; if 
\i flag
\i0  is NO, tracking ends when the mouse is dragged after the initial mouse down.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 This method first invokes 
\b startTrackingAt:inView:
\b0 .  If that method returns YES, then as mouse-dragged events are intercepted, 
\b continueTracking:at:inView:
\b0  is invoked, and, finally, when the mouse leaves the bounds or if the mouse button goes up, s
\b topTracking:at:inView:mouseIsUp:
\b0  is invoked (if 
\i cellFrame
\i0  is NULL, then the bounds are considered infinitely large).  You usually override one or more of these methods to respond to specific mouse events.  \

\fs14 \

